 "work_package": "O4a (Phase C wave 4): OpenSWATH extraction and SWATH windows",
 "method": "Port of ANALYSIS/OPENSWATH ChromatogramExtractorAlgorithm, ChromatogramExtractor, PeakMapExtractor, SwathWindowLoader, SwathQC and (partially) SwathMapMassCorrection. Every class-test section at the pin is transcribed with its literals (TEST_REAL_SIMILAR replayed at relative/absolute 1e-5). An oracle driver linking the executed C++ Release build printed, as %.17g, every value of the class-test flows plus edge cases (top-hat walk quirks, SWATH-window files with blank lines, CRLF, extra and missing columns, the full isSubsampledSpectrum_ grid, charge distributions for five sample counts and two tolerances, estimateWindow over eight residual sets, the SwathMapMassCorrection defaults, findSwathMapsPasef); the Rust tests replay those records bit for bit, except where a documented native difference refuses a file the C++ misreads. The driver ran twice in fresh processes with a clean environment; both record streams are byte-identical (results/differ.txt is empty).",
 "evidence_tier": "tier 1 (executed C++ Release on ibminode06, x86_64 Linux, gcc 14.4.0, install openms4-release-bc9cc12-c19e494-174b576: the oracle_* tests of tests/openswath_extraction.rs); tier 3 (transcribed class-test literals of the six *_test.cpp); tier 4 (native guards and derived invariants). ChromatogramExtractor_input.TraML is transcribed into a LightTargetedExperiment because TraMLFile and convertTargetedExp are not ported; the oracle prints the converted experiment and oracle_prepare_coordinates checks the transcription against it.",
